From: super_lite_music_player
Subject: [PATCH] include <cstdint> for GCC 13

upmpdcli 1.5.12 predates GCC 13, which stopped pulling <cstdint> in
transitively through other libstdc++ headers. Four headers use int64_t
and friends without asking for them, so against the GCC 13.4 toolchain
Buildroot 2025.02.9 builds, the package does not compile:

    src/upmpdutils.hxx:56:9: error: 'int64_t' does not name a type

Everything after that is a knock-on from the same cause - the member
declaration fails, so every later reference to UpSong::Res::size fails
too, which makes the error list look much worse than the fix.

Adding the include is what upstream did. Carried here rather than
bumping the package version, because the version is Buildroot's to
choose and this is the only thing wrong with it.

Signed-off-by: super_lite_music_player
diff -Naur up-a/src/conftree.h up-b/src/conftree.h
--- a/src/conftree.h
+++ b/src/conftree.h
@@ -49,6 +49,7 @@
  * (useful to have central/personal config files).
  */
 
+#include <cstdint>
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <map>
 #include <string>
diff -Naur up-a/src/mediaserver/cdplugins/netfetch.h up-b/src/mediaserver/cdplugins/netfetch.h
--- a/src/mediaserver/cdplugins/netfetch.h
+++ b/src/mediaserver/cdplugins/netfetch.h
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
 #ifndef _MEDIAFETCH_H_INCLUDED_
 #define _MEDIAFETCH_H_INCLUDED_
 
+#include <cstdint>
 #include <functional>
 
 #include "bufxchange.h"
diff -Naur up-a/src/readfile.h up-b/src/readfile.h
--- a/src/readfile.h
+++ b/src/readfile.h
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 #ifndef _READFILE_H_INCLUDED_
 #define _READFILE_H_INCLUDED_
 
+#include <cstdint>
 #include <sys/types.h>
 
 #include <string>
diff -Naur up-a/src/upmpdutils.hxx up-b/src/upmpdutils.hxx
--- a/src/upmpdutils.hxx
+++ b/src/upmpdutils.hxx
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 #ifndef _UPMPDUTILS_H_X_INCLUDED_
 #define _UPMPDUTILS_H_X_INCLUDED_
 
+#include <cstdint>
 #include <string>
 #include <unordered_map>
 #include <vector>
